COSMOS GEN-CONVOY §6 lock-wait extension (docs/COSMOS-GEN-CONVOY-DESIGN.md) — main-thread engine-lock
acquire-WAIT probe, compile-gated + runtime-gated, byte-off.

The Build-#1 alloc probe FALSIFIED alloc-stall as dominant (~14%); the remaining ~86% of the walk spike is
main-thread stall on a NON-malloc engine lock while workers flood generation (wf_vox_gen 51x, pool 6). This
times the MAIN-THREAD acquire wait on the two lock families the streaming/query path holds — RWLock
(VoxelData::Lod::map_lock) and Mutex (ThreadedTaskRunner completed/staged) — surfacing wf_lock_rwlock_ms /
wf_lock_mutex_ms.

Reuses the ZN_VOX_ALLOC_PROBE compile gate (godot/0003 `alloc_probe`; no new build knob). Runtime flag
FP_GEN_LOCK_PROBE (cosmos setup gen_lock_probe). ABSENT gate => rw_lock.h/mutex.h byte-identical, lock_probe
empty. IMPORTANT: util/thread/ is NOT globbed by common.py (each .cpp is listed explicitly), so the new
util/thread/lock_probe.cpp is registered in common.py:get_sources() (mirrors patch 0007's mechanism) — WITHOUT
this the wrappers link-fail with undefined zn_lock_probe_begin/end. Applies on top of godot_voxel 0015 + 0016.
diff --git a/util/thread/lock_probe.h b/util/thread/lock_probe.h
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/util/thread/lock_probe.h
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+#ifndef ZN_LOCK_PROBE_H
+#define ZN_LOCK_PROBE_H
+
+// VOXIVERSE COSMOS GEN-CONVOY (docs/COSMOS-GEN-CONVOY-DESIGN.md §6 lock-wait extension) — main-thread
+// lock-acquire WAIT probe. Extends the godot/0003 alloc-probe technique to the engine locks the streaming/
+// query path acquires while the voxel workers are busy: the Build-#1 probe FALSIFIED alloc-stall as the
+// dominant cause (~14 %), so the remaining ~86 % of the walk spike is main-thread stall on something that is
+// NOT malloc / NOT apply / NOT render. Prime suspects (census): the VoxelData per-LOD RWLock (`map_lock`,
+// storage/voxel_data.h:364) held write by the main streaming/apply path while it inserts generated blocks
+// and read by the query/collision path, and the ThreadedTaskRunner mutexes drained on main while 6 workers
+// push completed generation tasks. On WASM the browser main thread cannot Atomics.wait, so a contended
+// acquire BUSY-SPINS on main — invisible to every existing bucket.
+//
+// This times the main-thread acquire WAIT per lock CLASS (RWLock vs Mutex) and accumulates it, surfaced via
+// VoxelEngine.get_stats() -> remote_bridge as wf_lock_rwlock_ms / wf_lock_mutex_ms (cumulative; the analysis
+// differences successive worst-frame snapshots). Compile-gated by ZN_VOX_ALLOC_PROBE (the same web scons
+// `alloc_probe` option godot/0003 adds — reused, no new build knob); ABSENT by default => this header is
+// empty and rw_lock.h/mutex.h are byte-identical. Runtime-gated by zn_set_lock_probe_enabled (flipped from
+// FP_GEN_LOCK_PROBE via cosmos setup) so it toggles independently of the alloc probe.
+//
+// The functions are OUT-OF-LINE (lock_probe.cpp) on purpose: rw_lock.h / mutex.h are hot low-level headers
+// included very early and widely, so they must NOT pull in core/os/thread.h or the OS ticks source (cycle
+// risk). They only see these declarations.
+
+#ifdef ZN_VOX_ALLOC_PROBE
+
+#include <cstdint>
+
+namespace zylann {
+
+enum ZnLockClass {
+	ZN_LOCK_RWLOCK = 0, // dominated by VoxelData::Lod::map_lock (the only hot main-acquired RWLock)
+	ZN_LOCK_MUTEX = 1, // dominated by the ThreadedTaskRunner completed/staged mutexes during a gen flood
+	ZN_LOCK_CLASS_COUNT = 2
+};
+
+// Returns a start tick if the probe is active (enabled AND caller is the main thread), else 0. When it
+// returns 0 the matching zn_lock_probe_end() is a no-op, so a worker-thread or disabled acquire pays only
+// one atomic load + a thread_local compare.
+uint64_t zn_lock_probe_begin();
+// Accumulates (now - t0) into the class bucket. No-op when t0 == 0.
+void zn_lock_probe_end(int lock_class, uint64_t t0);
+
+// Runtime master switch (default false). Flipped from FP_GEN_LOCK_PROBE via cosmos setup, main thread.
+void zn_set_lock_probe_enabled(bool enabled);
+// Cumulative main-thread acquire-wait for a class, in milliseconds (usec/1000). For the stats surface.
+double zn_lock_probe_wait_ms(int lock_class);
+// Cumulative main-thread acquire count for a class (sanity / rate).
+uint64_t zn_lock_probe_count(int lock_class);
+
+} // namespace zylann
+
+#endif // ZN_VOX_ALLOC_PROBE
+
+#endif // ZN_LOCK_PROBE_H
diff --git a/util/thread/lock_probe.cpp b/util/thread/lock_probe.cpp
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/util/thread/lock_probe.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@
+#include "lock_probe.h"
+
+// VOXIVERSE COSMOS GEN-CONVOY §6 lock-wait extension. Implementation lives here (out-of-line) so the hot
+// headers rw_lock.h / mutex.h stay free of core/os includes. Entirely compiled out when the probe scons
+// option is off (ZN_VOX_ALLOC_PROBE undefined) => byte-identical stock.
+#ifdef ZN_VOX_ALLOC_PROBE
+
+#include <core/os/os.h> // OS::get_singleton()->get_ticks_usec()
+#include <core/os/thread.h> // ::Thread::is_main_thread()
+
+#include <atomic>
+
+namespace zylann {
+
+namespace {
+std::atomic<bool> g_lock_probe_enabled{ false };
+std::atomic<uint64_t> g_lock_wait_usec[ZN_LOCK_CLASS_COUNT];
+std::atomic<uint64_t> g_lock_count[ZN_LOCK_CLASS_COUNT];
+} // namespace
+
+uint64_t zn_lock_probe_begin() {
+	if (!g_lock_probe_enabled.load(std::memory_order_relaxed)) {
+		return 0;
+	}
+	// Only main-thread acquire WAIT matters: on WASM the browser main thread busy-spins on a contended lock
+	// (no Atomics.wait), which is the stall we are hunting. Worker waits are off the felt-frame path.
+	if (!::Thread::is_main_thread()) {
+		return 0;
+	}
+	const OS *os = OS::get_singleton();
+	if (os == nullptr) {
+		return 0;
+	}
+	const uint64_t t = os->get_ticks_usec();
+	return t != 0 ? t : 1; // 0 is the "inactive" sentinel; clamp a genuine 0 tick to 1
+}
+
+void zn_lock_probe_end(int lock_class, uint64_t t0) {
+	if (t0 == 0) {
+		return;
+	}
+	if (lock_class < 0 || lock_class >= ZN_LOCK_CLASS_COUNT) {
+		return;
+	}
+	const OS *os = OS::get_singleton();
+	if (os == nullptr) {
+		return;
+	}
+	const uint64_t now = os->get_ticks_usec();
+	const uint64_t dt = now > t0 ? now - t0 : 0;
+	g_lock_wait_usec[lock_class].fetch_add(dt, std::memory_order_relaxed);
+	g_lock_count[lock_class].fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed);
+}
+
+void zn_set_lock_probe_enabled(bool enabled) {
+	g_lock_probe_enabled.store(enabled, std::memory_order_relaxed);
+}
+
+double zn_lock_probe_wait_ms(int lock_class) {
+	if (lock_class < 0 || lock_class >= ZN_LOCK_CLASS_COUNT) {
+		return 0.0;
+	}
+	return double(g_lock_wait_usec[lock_class].load(std::memory_order_relaxed)) / 1000.0;
+}
+
+uint64_t zn_lock_probe_count(int lock_class) {
+	if (lock_class < 0 || lock_class >= ZN_LOCK_CLASS_COUNT) {
+		return 0;
+	}
+	return g_lock_count[lock_class].load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
+}
+
+} // namespace zylann
+
+#endif // ZN_VOX_ALLOC_PROBE
